From: Smartisan ODIN mainline porting effort
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] msm8953: drop markw and rosy from the QCDT device table

Force lk2nd to pick the Smartisan ODIN entry.

Why this is needed: lk2nd's QCDT table holds both
msm8953-smartisan-odin (board-id <0x0b 0x01>) and
msm8953-xiaomi-markw (<0x1000b 0x01>). VARIANT_MASK is 0xff, so both
have variant_id 0x0b -- the 0x10 nibble is only the variant *major*,
which loses to SUBTYPE_EXACT_MATCH. Both carry subtype 0x01, so the
tie-break falls through to comparing variant_major, and markw can win.

markw requires an exact major match while odin only needs
MAJOR_BEST, so once markw is gone odin is the only SUBTYPE_EXACT
candidate left and wins outright.

This patch builds the "nomarkw" lk2nd image: 27 appended DTBs
instead of 29, and `strings lk2nd.img | grep xiaomi-markw` == 0.

Apply only 0001-0003 for the full (untrimmed) image.
--- a/lk2nd/device/dts/msm8953/rules.mk	2026-08-29 23:46:29
+++ b/lk2nd/device/dts/msm8953/rules.mk	2026-08-29 23:46:29
@@ -19,14 +19,12 @@
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/msm8953-wingtech-wt89536.dtb \
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/msm8953-xiaomi-common.dtb \
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/msm8953-xiaomi-daisy.dtb \
-	$(LOCAL_DIR)/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dtb \
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/msm8953-xiaomi-oxygen.dtb \
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/msm8953-xiaomi-vince.dtb \
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/sda450-samsung-r05.dtb \
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/sdm450-motorola-ali.dtb \
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/sdm450-mtp.dtb \
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/sdm450-samsung-r04.dtb \
-	$(LOCAL_DIR)/sdm450-xiaomi-rosy.dtb \
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/sdm632-fairphone-fp3.dtb \
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/sdm632-mtp.dtb \
 	$(LOCAL_DIR)/sdm632-mtp-3.dtb \
